{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"f8e7f94b33677aae","type":"text","text":"Or single pulse then detuning second transmon to lock leakage.","x":-115,"y":439,"width":242,"height":98},
		{"id":"1e106c4cb42360ca","type":"text","text":"Continuous pulse on the second transmon to populate it with dissipation.","x":-501,"y":300,"width":278,"height":92},
		{"id":"5db109f14f136000","type":"text","text":"This could remove leakage from the coupler?","x":-501,"y":611,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"57abf11fd641a7b9","type":"text","text":"Very fast","x":-501,"y":709,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"66d9e2518195e1fc","type":"text","text":"Single pulse and then fast reset?","x":-487,"y":458,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ac142c7b24a2d095","type":"text","text":"# Idle Leakage Dynamics and Readily Available Leakage Removal in Tunable Coupler QPUs","x":-1160,"y":-560,"width":508,"height":155,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"7ef51744a66bf6cd","type":"text","text":"### We can use readily available hardware on tunable coupler QPUs for PASSIVE leakage removal.","x":-933,"y":9,"width":320,"height":140,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"bc1efb663ee61b7f","type":"text","text":"Leakage removal with qubits on resonance, empty second site.","x":-906,"y":223,"width":265,"height":86,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"36f25d2ef788276c","type":"text","text":"Leakage removal with single excitations on the second transmon","x":-906,"y":371,"width":260,"height":91,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"56d46dade7fe67c9","type":"text","text":"Unrealistic one with coupler |2> on resonance.","x":-906,"y":543,"width":254,"height":81,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"147863a75aa026f6","type":"text","text":"How does it depend on the state of the second qubit?","x":-2848,"y":292,"width":250,"height":74,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"5a7ef619263c0963","type":"text","text":"Show also for having excitation on the second site","x":-2848,"y":645,"width":250,"height":64,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a8aec5f18d234f5f","type":"text","text":"### The coupler can turn off the qubit interaction and allow leakage mobility $|200\\rangle \\rightarrow |002\\rangle$.  ","x":-2528,"y":-14,"width":320,"height":140,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"4c0aa86475598092","type":"text","text":"Why does this happen if effective coupling is zero?","x":-2493,"y":303,"width":250,"height":63,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"c0f1985a0db70cfd","type":"text","text":"Derive analytical expression for $|200\\rangle \\rightarrow |002\\rangle$ and $|201\\rangle \\rightarrow |102\\rangle$. Also derive these when assuming $w_1 \\neq w_2$ .","x":-2493,"y":624,"width":250,"height":153,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"55b0e8cd5d8bff7d","type":"file","file":"Coupler LRU/PaperSchemeFigures/CouplerFilterPlot.png","x":-3280,"y":846,"width":381,"height":400},
		{"id":"734863e282ede178","type":"text","text":"Show that while the qubit interaction is not happening, leakage interaction is!","x":-3215,"y":639,"width":250,"height":111,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"cd3dfb8a2838f5bc","type":"text","text":"Does it really? ","x":-3214,"y":292,"width":250,"height":67,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"d51bc84319d70831","type":"text","text":"How fast is the interaction?","x":-3024,"y":450,"width":250,"height":50,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"3098db2f85e08895","type":"text","text":"Under what conditions does it happen? When does it not?","x":-2160,"y":281,"width":250,"height":87,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"e266974ab4222dd8","type":"text","text":"Tunneling can also be relevant.","x":-2160,"y":489,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"8d4c2cc5592451c5","type":"text","text":"Typically the conditions for this are met. So what is the point?","x":-1802,"y":284,"width":257,"height":84,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b7d38912544c66f6","type":"text","text":"Enables leakage removal possibilities!","x":-1798,"y":469,"width":250,"height":59,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c64b6f67901e24e2","type":"text","text":"There can be leakage in the coupler, does it also move? Does it affect the leakage moving?","x":-1460,"y":281,"width":237,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"f92adab936c57a61","type":"text","text":"Show time dynamics for $|010\\rangle$, $|110\\rangle$, $|210\\rangle$.","x":-1585,"y":739,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b162fce2dea5f62f","type":"file","file":"Coupler LRU/PaperSchemeFigures/CouplerSingleExcPlot.png","x":-1660,"y":1054,"width":400,"height":400}
	],
